<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BC">Example <span data-tag="06BC">7.6.6.9</span>.</a> Following the convention of Remark <a data-tag="03PU" href="/tag/03PU">4.9.0.4</a>, an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is complete (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06B7" href="/tag/06B7">7.6.6.1</a>) if and only if it is $ \Omega $-complete (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03UD" href="/tag/03UD">7.6.6.6</a>), where $ \Omega $ is a fixed strongly inaccessible cardinal. Similarly, a functor $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is continuous (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06BA" href="/tag/06BA">7.6.6.4</a>) if and only if it is $ \Omega $-continuous. </p>
